Issue #12 item U1 -- mutation evidence (INV-7)
================================================================================

Base commit (parent of this item's own commit): fd46fed0db06aa3f66f3dda7aada8dff18f31ee3

What was mutated and how
-------------------------
One temporary edit to `crates/corvette-ui/src/dashboard.rs`, reverted after
capture (confirmed by `diff` against the pre-mutation file showing no
residue, and by `git status`/`git diff` showing only this item's own real
changes afterward): the go2rtc `<iframe src="/live/webrtc/webrtc.html?src=...">`
this item's own Do step 1 removed was reintroduced, mounted alongside (not
instead of) the new `<LiveCameraTile>` inside the same `<article
class="camera-card">`:

    {cameras.into_iter().map(|camera| {
        let player_url = format!(
            "/live/webrtc/webrtc.html?src={}",
            camera.name,
        );
        let player_title = format!("{} live video", camera.display_name);
        view! {
            <article class="camera-card">
                <iframe
                    class="camera-player"
                    src=player_url
                    title=player_title.clone()
                    allow="autoplay; fullscreen"
                ></iframe>
                <LiveCameraTile camera_name=camera.name.clone() title=player_title/>
                <h2>{camera.display_name}</h2>
                <p>{camera.name}</p>
            </article>
        }
    }).collect_view()}

This exercises exactly the defect this item's own Mutation text names --
"reintroduce the iframe rendering path" -- against two independent oracles:
the extended `scripts/check_no_go2rtc.sh` (a static source-text check, INV-7)
and a real headless-browser Playwright assertion that no `<iframe>` element
is present on the rendered page
(`tests/ui/live_view.spec.cjs`, "the grid tile renders no iframe, with or
without a live media-bridge endpoint" -- deliberately written to need only a
mocked `/api/config` response, not a live `corvette-media-bridge` fixture, so
it runs unconditionally as part of a plain `make check-ui`).

